{"agent_id":"pp3g-T2OR-planning-task-zero-context-plan-revision-only-no-290d","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-14T22:50:53.363896025Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"3c49b50b-e2f5-4bec-98f4-1a64ed991b1f","comment_uuid":"a5e8cfd0-b68f-43d3-97d3-0fc6dae81457","author":"pp3g-T2OR-planning-task-zero-context-plan-revision-only-no-290d","content":"# REVISED REMEDIATION PLAN — Tools-migration blockers B1–B6 (round-2 revision per C1–C4)\n\nZERO-CONTEXT planning revision. Read-only: no files modified, no commits. Base: #361 result comment. Reviews consumed: #362 (Luna), #363 (Big Pickle), #364 (Mimo). All three verdicts CHANGES REQUESTED; all C1–C4 claims re-verified on disk 2026-08-14 before revision. New evidence beyond #361 is marked [NEW].\n\n## EVIDENCE RE-VERIFIED / NEW (used in this revision)\n\n- [NEW] Fork init source (~/projects/crosslink/crosslink/src/commands/init/mod.rs) — exact semantics confirmed:\n  - Plain `init` on an initialized repo: early-return `Ok` with NO writes (mod.rs:869–874, \"Already initialized\"), test_run_already_initialized_no_force:1334.\n  - `init --update`: deleted files are skipped (\"deleted by user, skipping (will not recreate)\", mod.rs:683–687), test_update_skips_deleted_files:2527.\n  - `init --force`: writes embedded HOOK_CONFIG_JSON over hook-config.json (mod.rs:989), rewrites `.crosslink/.gitignore` (mod.rs:1012) and root `.gitignore` managed section (mod.rs:1040, merge.rs:57–91), rewrites ALL 31 RULE_FILES including global.md/knowledge.md/project.md (mod.rs:1045–1059; RULE_FILES generated from resources/crosslink/rules/, 31 entries), rewrites hooks/mcp/commands/skills (mod.rs:1075–1142), writes init-manifest (mod.rs:1144–1149). test_run_force_updates_rules:1633 proves a user-modified global.md is restored to embedded.\n  - [NEW] `write_mcp_json_merged` (merge.rs:96–152) is a MERGE, not an overwrite: preserves user mcpServers + top-level keys, overwrites colliding keys with embedded (with warnings), re-serializes alphabetically; REFUSES to overwrite invalid existing JSON (merge.rs:106–110). So `.mcp.json` is not destroyed by --force — for Tools/ASES (same 3 servers, verified 453B each) the merge is semantically a no-op.\n  - [NEW] Tools' `.crosslink/hook-config.json` is SEMANTICALLY IDENTICAL to embedded (both re-serialize to 2041B; only raw key order differs). The --force clobber is therefore benign formatting churn for Tools, but DESTRUCTIVE for ASES/tripn, whose values genuinely differ (ASES comment_discipline=encouraged/signing_enforcement=audit; tripn required/enforced — re-verified).\n  - Restore-set files are ALL git-tracked in Tools AND ASES (.crosslink/rules/{global,knowledge,project}.md, .crosslink/hook-config.json, .mcp.json) → `git restore` is a valid restore mechanism after --force. kickoff.md (ASES-only) and tooling.md are NOT in RULE_FILES → --force does not touch them.\n- [NEW] C3 state: Tools `git status --porcelain` = `M .crosslink/rules/global.md` (the \"Memory awareness\" nohup rule, +1 line), `M scripts/claude` (memory-scope systemd-run wrapper, which still carries the ${PROMPT:+\"\"} quoting bug), untracked `.opencode/`, `.worktrees/`, `.claude/findings-interrupt-plugin.md` — none gitignored (check-ignore exit 1). `.claude/hooks/` IS gitignored (managed section) → S1 confirmed.\n- [NEW] Sync write-set tracking: Tools plugins/scripts/skills tracked & clean; ASES/tripn `.opencode/plugins/*.ts` tracked (ls-files) & clean; ASES `.claude/skills/crosslink-*/SKILL.md` tracked; `~/.local/bin` NOT a git repo.\n- [NEW] Skills write-set divergence (not in #361): Tools/skills/crosslink-subagent-orchestration/SKILL.md = 4077B vs ASES = 6571B — ASES copy is a functional superset (adds the Task-tool vs kickoff decision matrix). crosslink-adversarial-review identical (2984B). The \"2 crosslink skills\" write-set has the SAME canonical-direction inversion as plugins/wrappers and must be canonicalized (ASES → Tools) before the first sync, exactly like D1/D2.\n- [NEW] C2 host: crosslink-guard.ts hooks `tool.execute.before` (:967) with lazily-resolved state in ensureState() (:829); ASES and tripn opencode.json both load `./plugins/*.ts` explicitly → the consumer check can hash the on-disk loaded file `<projectDir>/.opencode/plugins/<name>.ts`.\n- [NEW] S2/NC-2 env: tripn hook-config verified strict (comment_discipline=required, signing_enforcement=enforced, orchestrator `git worktree remove` gated at :59). bun at ~/.bun/bin/bun; opencode wrapper at ~/.local/bin/opencode; crosslink binary = 0.9.0-beta.1+37789b51-dirty (matches fork HEAD). No sync-tooling.sh exists anywhere (Tools/scripts, Tools/, ASES/ checked).\n- Wrappers re-verified: live claude 3039B (--agent :17, --auto :22, CROSSLINK_AGENT_TYPE :76, correct \"$PROMPT\" :80) vs Tools 2443B (quoting bug :68,:70, no --agent); live opencode 3639B (#274 FORK_MARKER fail-closed guard) vs Tools 1498B (no guard); crosslink-moe identical 5853B.\n- Plugin sizes: ASES crosslink-guard 42140B / tripn 37584B / Tools 33476B; orchestrator-guard ASES 3816B vs Tools+tripn 2367B; rtk-guard identical 13893B.\n\n---\n\n# 1. WHAT CHANGED vs #361 — PER C1–C4\n\n## C1 — B4 step-5 init sequence: REVISED (mechanics fixed)\n\n**Change: drop the `rm -rf` entirely; invoke `crosslink init --force` as the sole redeploy action; then restore the layer-owned restore set; then post-init hash-verify. Name the exact invocation and the restore set.**\n\nRationale (grounded in mod.rs):\n1. `--force` unconditionally rewrites all hooks/commands/mcp/skills (mod.rs:1075 `if !claude_exists || force`) — so the `rm` adds ZERO functional value. Its only effect is to make the sequence non-atomic: if `--force` aborts mid-way (e.g., `write_mcp_json_merged` refuses on invalid existing JSON, merge.rs:106–110, or any write error), a rm-first sequence leaves Tools with NO hooks — the exact bare-rm hazard B4 exists to prevent. Without the rm, a failed --force leaves the old working hooks in place (retryable, no broken window).\n2. The reviewers' plain-init hazard is real: `rm` + plain `init` = no-op (mod.rs:869–874) → no hooks. `rm` + `init --update` = deleted files skipped (mod.rs:683–687) → still no hooks. Only `--force` redeploys. So the revision names `--force` explicitly.\n3. The D3 \"remove embedded snapshots\" intent is preserved semantically: after --force the snapshot files exist but are documented as binary-deployed (remain gitignored); the pin+document step (below) is what removes the \"Tools fs carries stale snapshots as if owned\" confusion. The rm act itself was never the point; the point is a verified, pinned redeploy.\n4. The sledgehammer collateral is handled by an explicit restore set, because every restore-set file is git-tracked (verified):\n\n**Exact step-5 invocation (Tools):**\n1. Pre-snapshot: record sha256 of the 4-file restore set {`.crosslink/rules/global.md`, `.crosslink/rules/knowledge.md`, `.crosslink/rules/project.md`, `.crosslink/hook-config.json`} (+ `.mcp.json` defensively — merge makes it a no-op today, but cheap insurance). Also record the pre-init hook behavior state.\n2. `crosslink init --force` (pinned binary 0.9.0-beta.1+37789b51-dirty).\n3. Restore set: `git restore .crosslink/rules/global.md .crosslink/rules/knowledge.md .crosslink/rules/project.md .crosslink/hook-config.json .mcp.json` — for Tools, the step-0 commit (see C3) carries the current global.md override so `git restore` recovers it; knowledge/project/hook-config/.mcp restore to their committed (pre-init) state.\n4. Post-init verify: (a) hooks exist and `work-check.py` contains the NEW `!= 2` logic; (b) `git status --porcelain .crosslink/rules/ .crosslink/hook-config.json .mcp.json` is CLEAN (restore succeeded); (c) re-hash the restore set — all 5 sha256 must equal the pre-snapshot; (d) settings.json still resolves all 6 hooks.\n5. Document the binary pin + behavior delta in TOOLING.md §16 (unchanged from #361's intent).\n\n**ASES mirror (step 5b, sequenced AFTER Tools — NC-3 adopted):** same sequence; restore set = {`.crosslink/rules/global.md`, `knowledge.md`, `project.md`, `.crosslink/hook-config.json`, `.mcp.json`} (ASES has all five tracked; kickoff.md is untouched — not in RULE_FILES). ASES values differ from embedded, so the hook-config restore is REAL here, not formatting.\n\nAlternatives considered: (a) keep rm + --force + backup-copy restore — rejected: rm adds a failure mode without value; git-restore from committed state is strictly cleaner than a backup dir and consistent with C4's git-only decision; (b) defer step 5 entirely — retained as documented fallback only if zero runtime-behavior change is required during the migration window.\n\n## C2 — B3 enforcement spec: COMPLETED (two artifacts, directionality, state machine)\n\n**Change: separate the two artifacts, define location+lifecycle, state one-directionality explicitly, and replace \"warn first, hard-fail after proven\" with an operational state machine with a deliberate promotion transition.**\n\n(a) **Marker-role separation (Big Pickle M2a resolved):**\n- **Source-side canonical manifest** — `Tools/plugins/.canonical-manifest.json` (+ one manifest per write-set root: `Tools/scripts/.canonical-manifest.json`, `Tools/skills/.canonical-manifest.json`). Lifecycle: TRACKED in Tools git, committed with every canonical update. Contents: per-file sha256 + source commit + timestamp. This is what `sync-tooling.sh --check` compares destination files against.\n- **Per-destination marker** — `<dest>/.opencode/plugins/.canonical-manifest.json` (plugins) / `<dest>/.claude/skills/.canonical-manifest.json` (skills) / `~/.local/bin/.canonical-manifest.json` (wrappers). Lifecycle: GITIGNORED (one line added to each destination root .gitignore OUTSIDE the crosslink managed section, so `init --force` preserves it — verified write_root_gitignore only manages its marked section), machine-local, written by sync-tooling.sh on every sync, NEVER generated by consumers (consumers only READ it — a destination-generated marker cannot become its own stale authority; Luna's concern). Not committing the marker avoids per-sync git churn and keeps B5's git-status gate meaningful.\n- The consumer startup check compares its own loaded file against the PER-DESTINATION marker only; `--check` compares destinations against the SOURCE manifest. Tools presence is not required at runtime (marker is local) — if Tools is unavailable, the consumer check still runs; only `--check` needs Tools.\n\n(b) **One-directionality (Big Pickle M2b / Mimo NC-6 resolved):**\n- Explicit statement: the consumer startup check detects ONLY destination-local edits (someone edits ASES/.opencode/plugins/crosslink-guard.ts → mismatch vs the local marker → banner/hard-fail). An unsynced SOURCE-side edit (someone edits Tools/plugins/crosslink-guard.ts and forgets to sync) is invisible at startup — consumers silently run the stale version. That direction is covered by `--check` (operator release checklist + preflight rule) AND by making sync-tooling.sh bidirectionally capable (NC-6):\n- **`sync-tooling.sh --check`** = on-demand preflight (distinct from the consumer check — Mimo NC-1 adopted): compares every destination file against the source canonical manifest; reports both directions — (i) destination ≠ canonical AND == last-pushed marker → stale destination (re-sync fixes); (ii) destination ≠ canonical AND ≠ last-pushed marker → LOCAL EDIT (report as such, never silent); (iii) source manifest missing/stale → report.\n- **`sync-tooling.sh --pull <dest> <file>`** = bidirectional fold-back: writes a destination-local-edit back into Tools canonical (after operator confirmation), then re-commits the manifest — this closes the D1 inversion loop: edit-ASES → next --check reports → --pull folds to Tools → sync pushes → all consumers converge. The consumer check alone does not fix the inversion; the bidirectional capability does (NC-6).\n\n(c) **State machine (Mimo BF-1 / C2c resolved) — \"proven\" made operational:**\n- **State 0 (no marker)** = pre-sync / never-synced: consumer check is a NO-OP (nothing to compare). First sync has no prior manifest — `--check` reports \"not yet synced\", not drift (Luna's first-sync concern).\n- **State 1 (warn)** = marker exists, NOT promoted: mismatch → log to /tmp/crosslink-guard.log + session banner, enforcement continues (no wedge).\n- **State 2 (hard-fail)** = marker exists AND `\"promoted\": true` in the marker: mismatch → the plugin THROWS on tool.execute.before (a hard block of the operation — the host-level refusal mechanism Luna demanded; a banner/log alone is not refusal). Every subsequent tool call stays blocked until re-sync or demote.\n- **Transition 1→2 = `sync-tooling.sh --promote <dest>`** — a DELIBERATE operator action, never automatic. The tool REFUSES to promote unless the last `--check` for that destination was clean (all files match canonical; exit 0), recorded as `last_check_ok` in the marker. \"Proven\" is therefore operationally: one clean `--check` + explicit `--promote`.\n- **Check-self failure semantics (chosen explicitly):** marker MISSING → fail-open (State 0 no-op — pre-sync, don't wedge sessions); marker CORRUPT/unreadable/invalid JSON → in State 2 fail-CLOSED (cannot verify ⇒ treat as drift ⇒ hard-fail — a corrupt marker in a promoted destination is the tamper/partial-write condition the check exists to catch); in State 1 (not promoted) corrupt marker → warn only.\n\n## C3 — Step-0 + B5 preconditions: REVISED (narrowed precondition + step-0 classification)\n\n**Change 1 (Big Pickle M3 / Luna / Mimo BF-2):** replace B5's \"git status --porcelain must be empty\" with the narrow precondition: **\"no uncommitted modifications to files in the sync write-set\"** in Tools and every destination. Write-set = {Tools/plugins/{crosslink-guard,orchestrator-guard,rtk-guard}.ts, Tools/scripts/{claude,opencode,crosslink-moe}, Tools/skills/crosslink-*/SKILL.md} for Tools; {.opencode/plugins/*.ts, .claude/skills/crosslink-*/SKILL.md} for ASES/tripn. Tools' untracked `.opencode/`, `.worktrees/`, `.claude/findings-interrupt-plugin.md` are OUTSIDE the write-set → they do NOT block sync (documented as machine-local/working artifacts; optionally gitignored later, not required). This kills the self-contradiction: step 0 no longer has to produce an empty porcelain.\n\n**Change 2 (Mimo BF-2 vs Big Pickle S4 — committed to commit-global.md, with justification):** step 0 commits `.crosslink/rules/global.md` ONLY and does NOT commit scripts/claude.\n- global.md commit: justified despite Mimo BF-2 because (a) the file is ALREADY tracked in Tools git — the delta is an edit to a tracked file, not a new introduction; (b) the commit is a per-path-classified BASELINE SNAPSHOT annotated \"Tools-local override — never a sync source\" (Luna's per-path classification + operator approval satisfied); B1's \"rules are not synced\" governs the sync MANIFEST, which excludes rules regardless of git history — no contradiction with the ownership map; (c) it makes C1's restore mechanically clean (`git restore` from the step-0 commit). If the operator prefers Mimo's stash instead, the C1 restore mechanism must switch to a pre-init backup copy of the restore set — noted as the operator option; commit is recommended.\n- scripts/claude NOT committed in step 0 (Big Pickle S4): step 1 replaces the whole file with the live copy (the uncommitted delta's value — memory scope — is already contained in live ~/.local/bin/claude, verified; and the delta also carries the quoting bug, which the live copy fixes). Step 1's replacement commit carries the wrapper delta.\n\n## C4 — B5 transaction machinery: DECIDED (git-only atomicity)\n\n**Change (Mimo BF-3 / Luna):** DROP the transaction log (`Tools/.sync-state/`), the backup dir (`Tools/.sync-backup/`), and `.sync-tmp` staging. Adopt git-only atomicity:\n- The script writes files directly (idempotent: ALWAYS overwrite a destination file whose content equals the last-pushed marker OR equals canonical; NEVER skip, NEVER .sync-tmp).\n- Atomicity = per-destination git: after a run, the operator reviews `git diff` in each destination and commits per repo. A later-repo failure leaves earlier repos committed — each repo is independently consistent; the destination markers record exactly what was pushed, so `--check` reports which repos synced. This is NOT a cross-repo transaction and we stop pretending it is (Luna's point): no distributed coordination is possible without per-repo gates; git-only makes each repo atomic + independently reviewable.\n- Local-edit protection preserved (NOT \"never skip\" for local edits): a destination file that differs from BOTH canonical AND the last-pushed marker entry is a LOCAL EDIT → the script REFUSES (fail loudly, exit non-zero, instruct: commit locally, `--pull` to fold back, or explicit `--force`). No silent clobber — this retains #361 B5.2 + Luna's requirement while staying idempotent for the normal case.\n- Rollback = per-repo `git revert`/`git reset` (tracked destinations) or re-sync from canonical (gitignored `~/.local/bin` and `~/.claude`-style non-repo paths). No `--rollback` flag. First-sync behavior: no marker → State 0 (see C2).\n- S5 (rollback must restore markers): moot under git-only — there is no --rollback; after a per-repo revert, `--check` reports the reverted file as drifted and the operator re-syncs or --pulls. Marker regeneration on every sync keeps this self-healing.\n\n## Non-blocking fold dispositions (all folded or explicitly mooted)\n\n- **S1** — ADOPTED: checksum `--check` is the PRIMARY acceptance gate for ALL destinations; `git status` is a secondary sanity check for tracked destinations only (ASES/tripn .opencode/plugins); for gitignored `.claude/hooks` and non-repo `~/.local/bin`, --check (and for hooks, the B4 verify step's NEW-logic grep + settings resolution) is the gate. Hooks are NOT in the sync write-set (crosslink-init-deployed), so --check does not cover them — B4's verify step does.\n- **S2** — ADOPTED: add a tripn-compat behavioral acceptance test — load ASES crosslink-guard.ts in a scratch repo configured with tripn's hook-config (comment_discipline=required, signing_enforcement=enforced, orchestrator gates git worktree remove — verified) before the first real tripn sync; extend the B2(d) dry-run to assert exactly 3 plugin writes and ZERO rules writes. Risk row added (R11).\n- **S5** — MOOT under C4 git-only (see C4).\n- **S6** — ADOPTED + hardened (Luna's \"hard refusal, not warning\"): `--include-rules` is scoped to an explicit allowlist = the 28 binary-distributed RULE_FILES only (+ optionally tooling.md); it FAILS LOUDLY (exit non-zero) if a destination layer-owned file (global/knowledge/project) differs from the source's layer-owned copy — i.e., never overwrites a diverged layer-owned file.\n- **S7** — ADOPTED: run the first deploy (Tools/scripts → ~/.local/bin) IMMEDIATELY after canonicalization (end of step 1), establishing the first marker baseline for the wrapper leg; step 3's wrapper leg then detects any later live edit instead of silently reverting it.\n- **NC-2** — ADOPTED: the contract battery runs in the LIVE environment (bun ~/.bun/bin/bun, opencode ~/.local/bin/opencode, crosslink 37789b51 all verified present), with the wrapper-under-test overlaid via a scratch PATH; recorded passing results become an implementation gate (Luna).\n- **NC-3** — ADOPTED: B4 ASES mirror sequenced strictly AFTER Tools (step 5b), each with its own verify; no simultaneity.\n- **NC-5** — ADOPTED: sync-tooling.sh lives at `Tools/scripts/sync-tooling.sh` (tracked, versioned with the repo, Tools-owned per the TOOLING.md map); its own sha256 is recorded in the source canonical manifest (dogfooded); maintenance = warehouse responsibility.\n- **N-1** — MOOT under C4 git-only (no .sync-tmp).\n- **N-2** — ADOPTED: battery item 4 gains an explicit literal-quote test case (prompt with spaces + special chars must arrive as ONE arg — probe wrapper dumps \"$1\").\n- **NC-4** — ADOPTED: TOOLING.md notes the 28/31 count is a point-in-time snapshot; the three-class ownership MAP is the durable artifact.\n- **NC-6** — ADOPTED via C2(b) bidirectional `--pull`.\n- **[NEW, from this revision]** — skills write-set inversion: the 2 crosslink skills must be canonicalized (ASES superset → Tools) in step 1 alongside wrappers, else the first skill sync would push the stale Tools 4077B copy over ASES' 6571B superset. crosslink-adversarial-review is already identical (2984B) — no-op.\n\n---\n\n# 2. COMPLETE REVISED PLAN (8-step ordering)\n\n**Step 0 — Preconditions (revised by C3)**\n- Per-path classification + operator approval of the Tools worktree: commit `.crosslink/rules/global.md` (baseline snapshot, annotated Tools-local override, never-sync-source). Do NOT commit scripts/claude (S4 — step 1 replaces it). Untracked `.opencode/`, `.worktrees/`, `.claude/findings-interrupt-plugin.md` are outside the write-set — documented, not blockers.\n- Record provenance snapshot (live wrapper bytes/hashes, plugin sizes + functional-superset evidence, fork binary identity 37789b51, skills superset evidence).\n- Run the B6 contract battery + plugin load test against LIVE env (NC-2). Gate: battery passes, recorded.\n\n**Step 1 — Wrapper + skills canonicalization (D2; revised by B6/S7/new-skills finding)**\n- Replace Tools/scripts/claude with live ~/.local/bin/claude (resolves the uncommitted delta + quoting bug); replace Tools/scripts/opencode with live (gains #274 guard). crosslink-moe already identical.\n- Canonicalize the 2 crosslink skills from ASES/.claude/skills → Tools/skills (ASES copy is the functional superset — new finding).\n- Re-run battery on the Tools copies; IMMEDIATELY run first deploy Tools/scripts → ~/.local/bin (S7) and write the first wrapper-leg marker baseline.\n- Commit on Tools repo (gated).\n\n**Step 2 — Guard-plugin canonicalization (D1; revised by B6)**\n- Copy ASES .opencode/plugins/{crosslink-guard,orchestrator-guard,rtk-guard}.ts → Tools/plugins/ (ASES superset: 42140B/75 refs/0 hardcoded paths vs tripn 37584B/42 refs; orchestrator-guard ASES 3816B vs 2367B — functional evidence, not size).\n- Plugin load test against a fixture hook-config; tripn-compat load test (S2) runs here or at step 6 pre-deploy. Commit on Tools repo.\n\n**Step 3 — sync-tooling.sh (D4; revised by B1/B2/B3/B5/C4)**\n- Lives at Tools/scripts/sync-tooling.sh (NC-5). Manifest: plugins (Tools/plugins → layer/.opencode/plugins + tripn/.opencode/plugins), wrappers (Tools/scripts → ~/.local/bin), 2 crosslink skills (Tools/skills → layer/.claude/skills). `rules/` EXCLUDED (B1). tripn leg targets live dirs, NOT `.ases/` (B2). Absent layer targets (EDASES/Execution) skipped with warning.\n- C2 artifacts: writes source canonical manifests (Tools/plugins|scripts|skills/.canonical-manifest.json, tracked) + per-destination markers (gitignored, written per sync); ships `--check` (bidirectional, C2b), `--pull` (fold-back, NC-6), `--promote` (state transition, C2c), `--include-rules` (S6-scoped allowlist + hard refusal).\n- C4 semantics: git-only atomicity — direct writes, always-overwrite canonical/marker-state files, REFUSE + fail loudly on local edits, no log/backup/tmp; per-destination operator commits; per-repo `git diff` review after each run.\n- First-run behavior: no markers → State 0; first sync writes markers; `--check` pre-first-sync reports \"not yet synced\", not drift.\n\n**Step 4 — TOOLING.md + knowledge page (D3/D5/D6/D7; folds)**\n- Source-of-truth map: own/mirror split + three-class rules ownership matrix (B1) + \"count is a snapshot, map is durable\" note (NC-4) + hook-config.json listed as layer-owned with residual-drift note.\n- STALE marker on tripn-astro bundle (D5). §16 fork section: call it a fork, external upstream, canonical embedded-resource source; binary pin + hook behavior delta (B4/C1).\n- Fix §1.1/§1.2 false-identical claims (B6); document ~/.local/bin deploy leg + wrapper marker baseline (S7).\n- sync-tooling.sh documented as Tools-owned canonical tooling (NC-5); bidirectional --check/--pull contract (NC-6).\n- Refresh `tooling` knowledge page.\n\n**Step 5a — Tools hook redeploy (B4; revised by C1)**\n- Pinned sequence (Tools): pre-snapshot restore-set hashes → `crosslink init --force` → `git restore` the 5-file restore set → verify (hooks NEW != 2 logic; rules/hook-config/mcp git-clean; restore-set hashes equal pre-snapshot; 6 settings.json hooks resolve). Alternative (defer) documented if zero behavior change required.\n\n**Step 5b — ASES hook mirror (B4; NC-3 adopted)**\n- Same pinned sequence, sequenced AFTER 5a + verification; restore set = ASES 5 files (hook-config restore is REAL — values differ from embedded).\n\n**Step 6 — Consumer wiring + enforcement (B3; revised by C2)**\n- Add the consumer marker check to crosslink-guard.ts (first-hook/ensureState path): State 0 no-op / State 1 warn / State 2 throw-on-mismatch (host-level refusal), corrupt-marker semantics per C2(c). Add one-line destination .gitignore entries for the marker files (outside the managed section).\n- Wire `sync-tooling.sh --check` into the preflight rule + operator release checklist (source-side drift, C2b).\n- Promote destinations (ASES/tripn) via `--promote` after one clean --check each (C2c). ASES keeps its own plugin copies until sync lands (D1) — now with drift VISIBLE instead of silent.\n\n**Step 7 — Acceptance/verification (NEW, closes the 8-step ordering)**\n- Run `--check` against all destinations: zero mismatches; markers promoted; startup drift smoke-test (tamper a destination plugin → State 2 block observed; restore → clean).\n- tripn-compat load test result recorded (S2); contract battery results recorded (NC-2/Luna gate); git-log audit of Tools canonical commits; TOOLING.md map matches disk.\n\n---\n\n# 3. UPDATED RISK REGISTER\n\n| # | Risk | L | I | Mitigation (delta vs #361) |\n|---|------|---|---|---------------------------|\n| R1 | Hook behavior change on re-init (returncode semantics) wedges sessions | Med | High | C1 pinned --force + restore set + post-init hash verify + scratch test; defer option retained |\n| R1m | **C1 mechanics: plain init/--update no-op leaves NO hooks; --force clobbers layer-owned rules + hook-config** | **High** | **High** | **C1: explicit --force invocation; git-restore restore set (all tracked — verified); post-init restore-set hash equality + git-clean check; test_run_force_updates_rules behavior proven in scratch first** (NEW row — the round-2 blocker) |\n| R2 | Wrong authoritative plugin copy canonicalized | Low | High | B6 provenance (functional superset, not size) + plugin load test; tripn-compat load test (S2) |\n| R3 | Sync clobbers layer rules overrides | High if rules synced | High | B1 rules excluded; S6 --include-rules allowlist + hard refusal on diverged layer-owned; C4 local-edit refusal |\n| R4 | Wrapper regression after canonicalization (quoting/agent) | Med | Med | B6 battery before/after (live env, NC-2); S7 first deploy immediately after canonicalization |\n| R5 | Crosslink binary staleness invalidates embedded-resource claims | Med | Med | B4 binary pin (37789b51) in TOOLING.md; md5 baseline check |\n| R6 | Tools uncommitted changes lost during cutover | Med | Med | Step 0 per-path classification + operator approval (C3); scripts/claude carried by step-1 replacement commit (S4) |\n| R7 | tripn plugins drift if tripn leg deferred | Med | Med | B2 direct-path sync; fallback: defer + document |\n| R8 | Enforcement wedges consumers if hard-fail too early | Med | Med | C2 state machine: State 1 warn → State 2 ONLY via clean --check + explicit --promote (measurable criteria — Luna) |\n| R9 | Absent layer targets (EDASES/Execution) break script | Low | Low | Skip + warn |\n| R10 | hook-config.json divergence persists (half the enforcement surface) | High | Med | Listed layer-owned; residual drift documented; NOT synced (destructive for ASES/tripn — verified values differ) |\n| R11 | **tripn-compat failure: ASES plugin breaks under tripn's stricter hook-config** | **Med** | **Med** | **S2 scratch load test with tripn's config (required/enforced/worktree-remove gate) BEFORE first tripn sync; dry-run asserts zero rules writes** (NEW row — S2) |\n| R12 | **Marker lifecycle drift: committed markers churn git status; stale/corrupt markers mislead --check** | **Low** | **Med** | **C2: markers gitignored + machine-local; consumers only READ; corrupt-in-State-2 fails closed; markers regenerated every sync** (NEW row — S5/marker lifecycle) |\n| R13 | **Skills sync pushes stale Tools copy over ASES superset** | **Med** | **High** | **Step 1 canonicalizes skills ASES→Tools before first skill sync; crosslink-adversarial-review already identical** (NEW row — new finding) |\n\n---\n\n# 4. REVISED CHEAPEST DISCRIMINATING TESTS\n\n- **C1 (B4):** scratch repo: (1) `crosslink init` (no force) on an initialized repo → hooks unchanged/none (proves the plain-init no-op the plan avoids); (2) `crosslink init --force` → hooks deployed with NEW `!= 2` logic, rules overwritten with embedded (proves the clobber the restore set must undo); (3) full sequence: pre-hash → --force → git restore → post-hash → all 5 restore-set hashes equal + git-clean. Cost: ~10 min. If (3) fails, abort step 5a in Tools.\n- **C2 (B3):** (1) 5-line sha256 compare (hash → tamper → mismatch exits non-zero); (2) scratch repo with marker: State 1 tamper → banner + log, session continues; State 2 (promote) tamper → tool.execute.before THROWS (block observed); corrupt-marker-in-State-2 → block; missing marker → no-op; (3) `--check` reports BOTH stale-destination and local-edit classes; `--promote` refuses without a prior clean `--check`. Cost: minutes–one session.\n- **C3 (step 0):** after step 0, `git status --porcelain` on Tools write-set paths is empty while untracked non-write-set paths remain (precondition machine-checks only the write-set). Cost: seconds.\n- **C4 (B5):** sync dry-run → zero writes, exact op list; tampered destination file → script REFUSES + exit non-zero (no clobber); re-run same state → no-op (idempotent); per-destination `git diff` review after real run shows exactly the synced files. Cost: minutes.\n- **S2 (tripn-compat):** load ASES crosslink-guard.ts under tripn's hook-config in scratch → no crash, enforcement behaves per required/enforced config; tripn-leg dry-run reports exactly 3 plugin writes + zero rules writes. Cost: minutes.\n- **S7 (deploy leg):** after step-1 first deploy, `--check` on ~/.local/bin → clean; then edit live claude → `--check` reports local-edit. Cost: minutes.\n- **N-2 (quoting):** battery item 4 with a prompt containing spaces + special chars → probe wrapper reports exactly ONE argument. Cost: seconds.\n\n---\n\n# 5. WHAT-NOT-TESTED\n\n- **`crosslink init --force` not executed anywhere** — all init-behavior conclusions come from reading fork source mod.rs/merge.rs + tests (test_run_force_updates_rules:1633, test_run_already_initialized_no_force:1334, test_update_skips_deleted_files:2527) + binary version string match (0.9.0-beta.1+37789b51-dirty). The C1 scratch test (below) is the first execution.\n- **sync-tooling.sh not built** — C2/C4 semantics (bidirectional --check/--pull, --promote state machine, git-only atomicity, local-edit refusal) are designed from verified file reality, not run. First-run/rollback behavior is specified, not executed.\n- **Consumer marker check not implemented** — plugin currently hooks tool.execute.before only (:967); the State 0/1/2 behavior is a design, not a running plugin.\n- **Plugin load under tripn's stricter hook-config not executed** (S2) — tripn config verified on disk; the load test is a pre-first-sync gate.\n- **Contract battery not executed** — live env deps verified present (bun, opencode, crosslink); battery results are an implementation gate, not yet recorded.\n- **Tools/ASES .mcp.json merge-equivalence asserted from source reading + identical content, not executed** (merge is a no-op for identical server sets, per merge.rs:96–152).\n- **B1 md5 matrix is a point-in-time snapshot** (NC-4): 28/31 binary-identical holds at check time; the three-class ownership map is the durable artifact.\n- **Cost/time estimates are planning estimates, not benchmarked.**","created_at":"2026-08-14T22:50:53.354911389Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:feJ5hpFKkeeFzwOIb/BJoSSGGp7CL5xDXR6bDflle68","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgoDyRkpqsSHXj4J7S3WBZCyY8gzzlDnkXxRJwGKXyxksAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA1M5TeL3vORuBBmR6FqxZLDCMTkehp0ghSMJ8ecOAb0K7Ob47pLjEvEBkqGHoslvECzjInpA2PHYrLOwjOa7nCA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:feJ5hpFKkeeFzwOIb/BJoSSGGp7CL5xDXR6bDflle68","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgoDyRkpqsSHXj4J7S3WBZCyY8gzzlDnkXxRJwGKXyxksAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLE+LEAQHHLVXVc9AS/J5iS9C+VtJ03ep54b8rLPK9RyCoGPe74PMazhA+BBYRxfFemBesMKlkjV4Gn7VqOvdwY="}
